<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carnatic Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1746–1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carnatic Wars were three conflicts in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in which the British and French East India Companies backed rival claimants to the Carnatic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive">Robert Clive</a>'s defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcot">Arcot</a> in 1751 and the British victory at Wandiwash in 1760 broke French power. The wars made the British company the leading European force in southern India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carnatic-wars.jpg" alt="Carnatic Wars" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Hayman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lord_Clive_meeting_with_Mir_Jafar_after_the_Battle_of_Plassey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
